// EXPECT: [E106]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 8, Col 12: 'std' is not a value. A module is named by the last segment of its path or by its alias, so 'std.math' is `math` here
// spec: §16 — a module is qualified by the last segment of its path or by its alias. This was
// E102 (the Annex's code for an attribute name) at "Ln 0, Col 0", advising "call 'math' directly".
import std.math

func main() i32 {
    return std.math.max(1, 2) - 2
}
